  "heading": "\\group",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{group}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\group]\nDeclares: G ::= (X, *, e) is \\monoid via (X, *, e)\nsatisfies:\n. forAll: x \"in\" G\n  then:\n  . exists: y \"in\" G\n    suchThat:\n    . x * y = e\n    . y * x = e\nEnables:\n. capability: x_ \"in\" G :<->: x_ is \\group.element:of{G}\n  written: \"x_? \\in G?\"\nDocumented:\n. called: \"group\"\n. description: \"A group is a monoid in which every element $x$ has an inverse\n                $y$, so that $x * y = e = y * x$. Equivalently it is an\n                associative structure with identity in which every element is\n                invertible; this makes it a quasigroup as well as a monoid.\"\nId: \"e4d7371d-29bd-431f-ab09-e114fe89e5cf\"",
